Thu Oct  8 19:15:29 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.0.11:
  * raise the Python floor: requires-python >= 3.8 -> >= 3.11, so
    Python 3.8-3.10 are no longer supported upstream
  * add Python 3.15 to the supported interpreter range
- Refresh registry.tar.zst: the Rust core is unchanged, but the
  vendored crates move to their next patch release (pyo3 0.29.2 ->
  0.29.3, cc 1.5.1 -> 1.6.0, either 1.18.0 -> 1.19.0, libc 0.2.189
  -> 0.2.190)
- Declare the maturin >= 1.0 floor stated in build-system requires

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Sep 30 08:20:18 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 1.0.10:
  * fix a reentrancy deadlock in update() when one hasher with
    max_threads>1 is shared between threads (gh#oconnor663/blake3-py#120)
  * Rust blake3 core 1.8.5 -> 1.8.7 (drops the arrayref dependency),
    pyo3 0.29.0 -> 0.29.2; hash output unchanged (BLAKE3 is frozen)
- Run the full upstream test suite in %check via %pytest_arch
  (adds python-pytest and python-numpy BuildRequires)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Jul 12 19:10:45 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Initial package python-blake3 1.0.9
  * Python bindings for the official Rust BLAKE3 cryptographic hash
